      "imageWidth": 1206,
      "imageHeight": 1612,
      "story": "The Santa Maria dei Fossi Altarpiece is a 1496-1498 painting by Pinturicchio, now in the Galleria nazionale dell'Umbria in Perugia. Unusually for an altarpiece, it is painted on canvas stretched over wooden panels.",
      "facts": [
        "It was commissioned for the high altar of the church of Santa Maria degli Angeli in Perugia, also known as Santa Maria dei Fossi.",
        "The reliefs on the Madonna's throne are inspired by those on ancient Roman sarcophagi, then being rediscovered as part of the Italian Renaissance, whilst behind it is an Umbrian landscape.",
        "However, he also placed it just before the painter's shift to a less inspired period in which he used compositions from his collection of drawings rather than inventing new ones."
      ],
